WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:04.390
<i>All the fish in the world suddenly 
disappeared from its waters,</i>

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:08.410
<i>and ten years have passed without 
the cause being determined.</i>

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:13.030
<i>In order to fulfill people's 
ardent desire to eat fish,</i>

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.090
<i>Japan devoted her science and technology 
resources to building space fish tanks,</i>

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:21.080
<i>and the fishermen in Onomichi 
started fishing in space.</i>

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.680
<i>Later, the Equal Employment 
Opportunity Law was strengthened,</i>

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.020
<i>giving women the right 
to go space fishing, too.</i>

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.950
<i>And so, six cadet space-fisherwomen were 
gathered from within the country and out!</i>

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:45.640
<b>Space Fish: Between the Sky and Sea</b>

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.850
<b>Gonna Fish in Space!</b>

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:09.180
<i>Grandma, Haru here.</i>

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:13.410
<i>I'm about to take my first step toward 
fulfilling my dream of being a space fisher!</i>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.380
<i>Fukuyama. Fukuyama.</i>

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.050
Miss, aren't you going to Onomichi? 
You need to change trains here!

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.460
Wait, miss!

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.710
I forgot my stuff!

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.720
Catch!

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.170
Strike!

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.780
Good job, ma'am!

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.490
<i>I want to help you eat the sushi 
you love so much,</i>

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:41.220
<i>so I'm gonna go to space and catch 
you a whole bunch of fish, okay?</i>

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.750
Wow, a rocket!

00:02:51.490 --> 00:02:53.270
The wind feels so nice.

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:55.510
I should take a pic and send it to Grandma.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.160
Oh, I'm sorry!

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.640
S-Sorry about that.

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.790
This place feels more urban than I expected.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.540
Then again, I can smell the salt in the air.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.390
I should send this one, too.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.210
Send

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.210
Grandma

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.210
Others

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.550
<b>Grandma</b>

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:17.900
There, all done.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.550
<b>Sending</b>

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:17.550
<b>Sent</b>

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.420
Onomichi Enomachi Street

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:25.520
There's plenty of time before 
I have to be at City Hall.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.770
<i>We apologize for the wait.</i>

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:36.520
<i>Thank you for using the 
Mount Senkoji Ropeway today.</i>

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.070
Hey!

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:46.160
Lots of temples, shrines, and shipyards here.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.760
Is that bridge over there 
the Shimanami Sea Road?

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.040
Oh, right.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:54.020
Wow, I can see it!

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:57.710
You can see the rocket 
from all the way out here?

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.610
The OnoFish II.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.790
Space fishers take it to...

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.120
I wanna ride it into space already!

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.110
I wanna fish!

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.090
I'm getting fired up now!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.000
Oh?

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.210
My grandma loves elegant cats like you.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.420
Hey, black cat!

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:41.810
Wait!

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.440
Hey!

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.540
You're actually waiting for me?

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.420
You're so smart.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.710
Even your friends are here.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:52.930
So cute.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.190
Okay, then!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.240
Say cheese.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.370
This breaks a cat lover's heart.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.630
What a fearsome technique.

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:13.990
Wait up!

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.410
I lost them!

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.210
Huh? Where am I?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.210
Wait, what?

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:25.660
I'm lost!

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:28.890
Onomichi City Hall

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.600
Space Fishery Dept.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.160
She's late.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.150
Thirty-five minutes late.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:44.130
What is Soramachi Haru doing?!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:46.360
Narumi-kun.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:50.480
Station employees say they saw a girl 
matching Soramachi's description

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.990
exit the ticket gates over two hours ago.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:54.420
That long ago?

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.960
Still can't get through to her phone?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.540
I've been trying, but no luck.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.920
Soramachi Haru

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.130
Uh...

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:05.010
Would you like us guys to help look for her?

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.390
You <i>guys</i>?

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.630
Did I say something weird?

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:09.310
O-Oh, it's fine!

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.180
Some high school girls these days 
talk like they're one of the guys.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.090
What?!

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:14.760
C-Calm down, Narumi-kun!

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:15.640
I'm perfectly calm!

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.680
Mitsurugi Makoto.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.420
Yes.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:25.970
And, uh...

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.120
Sakura Maiko.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.030
Ye cannae e'en remember me name, eh?

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.530
Sorry, sorry.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.990
Anyway, it's the first time in 
Onomichi for both of you, right?

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:36.440
Right.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:39.390
We can't have you getting lost, too.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.460
Let's sit tight and wait a bit longer.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.550
My phone battery's dead,

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.360
and I'm all sweaty and gross.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:51.980
Hey, I can change in there.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.850
Onomichi Space Fishery Union

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:57.930
Why won't you let us go space fishing?!

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.660
You aren't ready for it yet.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:01.520
Go home.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:06.600
But we're just as good as the men 
at piloting flying fish and fishing!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.990
Them's fighting words.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:18.380
It'll be a million years before girls 
are ready to go space fishing!

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.750
Get outta here!

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.000
What's with that look?

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:27.190
Kagitani-kun, keep it cool.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:29.030
The Union Chief is right.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.090
Knock it off, Kagitani.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.630
Kazamatsuri.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:37.060
You give it a rest too, mis—no, Namino-san.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:40.280
Trainees can't go space fishing. 
It's too dangerous.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.520
There you have it.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.340
Besides, I only see the two of you here.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:47.020
Space fishing requires teams of three.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:51.070
I'm amazed you can say you wanna 
go when you don't even know that.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:51.740
Kagitani!

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:55.780
Drop it, Namino! We're leavin' for today!

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:58.740
Um...

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:03.170
Sorry to interrupt, but could you tell me 
how to get to Onomichi City Hall?

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.410
Huh? Who're you?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.630
From here,

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:10.220
take the train to Onomichi Station 
and follow the coast, and it's right there.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:14.090
What? But I walked here 
from Onomichi Station!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:14.620
Huh?

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:17.800
Onomichi
Space Fishery Union

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.800
Man, where did I mess up?

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:21.500
Thank you very much.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:23.600
Wait.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:28.230
You're one of the cadet space-fishers, right?

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.690
Yeah. I'm Soramachi Haru.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:33.180
You're from Mukaishima, right?

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.810
Huh? Uh...

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:38.450
I'm from Mukojima, not Mukaishima...

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.450
What're you grumblin' about?

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.950
If you're from Mukaishima, 
you must be good at swimming!

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.370
Yep. I've even won Nationals.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.630
How're you with flying fish?

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.350
Flying fish?

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.500
Oh, I love them. It's cool how they're like birds.

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:54.570
That's that, then!

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.290
There are three of us now.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:58.930
Let us go space fishing!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.310
Th-That's...

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.020
If you wanna go that badly, why not?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.300
Kagitani?

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.680
There, there.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:10.280
It's our chance to nip the 
girls' squad in the bud.

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:12.190
But this is too risky.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:15.620
I'll risk my life to save them 
if things go south, okay?

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.350
Uh, I need to get going to City Hall...

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.610
We're about to head to a space fish tank.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:25.500
Come with us.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.420
Huh?

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.090
Onomichi City Hall

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.500
What?!

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:35.060
Soramachi Haru's leaving to go space 
fishing with Namino and Makiko?!

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:37.960
Are you all right?

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:38.970
Hang in there!

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.700
You're speaking to Mannen now.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:45.720
Union Chief, Soramachi Haru's a total newbie! 
She hasn't undergone any training yet!

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.390
Stop her at once!

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:48.570
You can't?

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:51.230
She's already in the rocket?!

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:56.470
<i>Second stage liquid oxygen 
and hydrogen systems are ready.</i>

00:09:56.470 --> 00:10:00.350
<i>Second stage liquid oxygen 
and hydrogen systems are ready.</i>

00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.090
<i>Launch deck water curtain start.</i>

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:04.370
<i>Launch deck water curtain start.</i>

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.170
<i>All systems ready.</i>

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:07.680
<i>All systems ready.</i>

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:08.780
<i>Main Engine ignition.</i>

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:10.610
<i>Main Engine ignition.</i>

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:11.940
<i>SRB ignition...</i>

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.300
<i>SRB ignition...</i>

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:14.730
<i>And lift off!</i>

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:15.990
<i>And lift off!</i>

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:28.530
<i>SRB jettison.</i>

00:10:28.530 --> 00:10:30.200
<i>SRB jettison.</i>

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:33.730
<i>Grandma...</i>

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:37.610
<i>For some reason, I'm going to space!</i>

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:45.740
Line up!

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:50.070
We're going over the fishing 
mission one more time.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:55.420
Hurry up! How long're you goin' ta take?!

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.650
But...

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.550
Relax. I'll help ya out.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.760
Thank you so much.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:04.510
Oh?

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.610
All done!

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:09.250
I've always dreamed of wearing 
one of these suits in space!

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.980
It's like I'm a real space fisher!

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.440
What're you talkin' about?

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:16.650
Thank you for earlier, uh...

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:19.770
I'm Maki Makiko, nineteen.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:21.230
And this is...

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:23.140
Murakami Namino, seventeen.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.650
Hey, I'm seventeen, too!

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:28.960
Phew, I thought you were the same age 
as Makimaki-san since you were so bossy.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.440
Why, you cheeky...

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:32.220
I didn't mean it that way.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:34.940
Also, she's Maki Makiko-san, not Makimaki-san.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:35.910
Right.

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.510
Makimaki's fine by me.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:39.720
To start off,

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:43.930
we're lending the girls' squad cadets 
on this mission three flying fish.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.870
They're the latest model of 
strike pods. Don't break 'em.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:52.850
<b>Watch your head</b>

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:52.850
Shimanami
Dock
Entrance

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.960
We'll be fishing in Tank 1.

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.850
Once we splash down, we'll use 
the fishfinder to detect any schools

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:55.660
and use the flying fish to catch them.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:57.570
Stay alert at all times.

00:11:58.090 --> 00:11:58.880
That is all.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.450
We'll hereby set sail for Tank 1.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.910
Wow, so this is a flying fish cockpit.

00:12:09.190 --> 00:12:12.260
<i>All of you pick a guardian 
deity on the way there.</i>

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:12.820
<i>Got it.</i>

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:15.380
Uh, what's a guardian deity?

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.550
Before you ask, I did read the primer.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.440
<i>This is ridiculous.</i>

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.380
<i>Sort it out by yourselves, girls' squad!</i>

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:28.850
Guardian deities are space-fishing 
partners who provide you support.

00:12:29.270 --> 00:12:32.470
Pick one from the God app.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:33.560
God app?

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:38.170
Wait, you haven't even downloaded the app 
that lets you summon guardian deities?

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.240
I guess not.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:40.970
You <i>guess</i>?!

00:12:40.970 --> 00:12:42.070
I don't believe you!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.280
Show me your phone.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.180
But...

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.700
The battery's dead, you see.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.300
All yours, Makiko-san.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:55.790
Here, use this spare battery.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:58.380
Thank you, Makimaki-san!

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.540
<i>T-minus 15 minutes to Tank 1.</i>

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.340
Er, she said to place my phone in the holder

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:08.610
and touch the buttons to my side, I think.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.230
Oh, the display lit up.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.500
Now for the side buttons...

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.020
<i>Looks like ya setup the phone all right.</i>

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.480
<b>Now for the side buttons...</b>

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:17.150
<b>What?</b>

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.150
<b>What?
How could you tell?</b>

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.480
<i>What? How could you tell?</i>

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:18.480
<b>What?
How could you tell?
(*_*;</b>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:22.220
<i>The button you touched just now is for comms.</i>

00:13:22.220 --> 00:13:26.380
<i>The deities make it possible to 
radio underwater at short distances.</i>

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:25.950
<b>The deities make it possible to 
radio underwater at short distances.
(-_-)</b>

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:29.660
<b>The button you touched
just now is for comms.
(^v^)</b>

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.370
<i>If that doesn't work, use this instead!</i>

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.240
<b>If that doesn't work,</b>

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:27.950
<b>If that doesn't work,
use this instead!</b>

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.660
<b>If that doesn't work,
use this instead!
(.>_<.)</b>

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:29.660
<i>Wow! That's so cool!</i>

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:28.780
<b>Wow!</b>

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:29.660
<b>Wow!
That's so cool! (^v^)</b>

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:32.500
<i>I know this is abrupt, but use the God app</i>

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:34.800
<i>to pick a deity from the Yaoyorozu Shrine.</i>

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:35.620
Roger!

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.120
I'm summoning Odin,

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.410
and Makiko-san will be summoning Kuraokami,

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:47.860
so pick anything other than those two.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.500
Anything other than Odin or Kuraokami, huh?

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:57.810
<b>Misaki-sama</b>

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:57.810
<b><i>Summon</i></b>

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:53.930
Cute!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.910
I choose you!

00:13:58.310 --> 00:14:04.780
<b><i>Summoning
Successful</i></b>

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:00.560
<i>I'm Misaki-sama!</i>

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:04.780
<i>Summoning me means you have 
a super-duper eye for picking deities.</i>

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:07.400
Aw, you're making me blush.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:08.740
I'm Haru.

00:14:09.060 --> 00:14:12.990
Wh-Why'd she have to go for 
the most useless one?

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.700
<i>What? Is it?!</i>

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.690
Makiko-san.

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:19.380
<i>Let's ignore her and fish by ourselves.</i>

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:20.810
R-Right.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:21.920
<i>No!</i>

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:25.080
<i>Don't worry about it, Haru. Believe in me.</i>

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:27.780
Yeah, can't take back my choice now.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:28.920
Let's do our best together.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:32.470
That bothers me a little bit, 
but that's the spirit!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.220
All right. Here we are.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:34.920
Yeah.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:37.250
So this is a space fish tank.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:39.970
<i>Detecting school up ahead!</i>

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:41.690
<i>All hands, prepare to launch!</i>

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:47.320
All units, take off!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:57.090
O-Oh, God, what do I do?

00:14:57.090 --> 00:14:58.490
<i>Calm down, Haru.</i>

00:14:58.490 --> 00:15:01.030
<i>Just follow my instructions,
and you'll be fine.</i>

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.170
B-But...

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.880
<i>When the signal in front turns green, 
let go of the right lever</i>

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:07.900
<i>and put the pedal to the metal!</i>

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.010
<i>Now!</i>

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:32.820
Hey, Misapyon.

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.670
<i>H-How can you call a deity that? 
Super-duper rude!</i>

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:37.610
What's the problem? It's cute.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:39.120
Anyway, look.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:42.580
Why are our flying fish glowing? 
What's with that light?

00:15:42.990 --> 00:15:45.260
When a fisher summons a deity,

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.540
their strike pod is engulfed in its aura,

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.920
<b>God App</b>

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:50.270
and its fishing tools 
become available to use.

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:51.750
A guardian deity's fishing tools?

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:54.820
What tools do you have, Misapyon?

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:55.720
None!

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:57.910
What? Why?

00:15:57.910 --> 00:15:59.750
<i>Let me finish.</i>

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:03.630
<i>Instead of tools, you get to locate 
space fish faster than the fishfinder</i>

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:05.960
<i>and gain better danger detection.</i>

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:07.790
Wow, you're awesome.

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.070
I am a deity, after all.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:09.990
Stay focused.

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:12.750
The fishfinder picked up a signal. 
The school's very close.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:13.760
<i>Roger.</i>

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.690
Hey, Misapyon. What happened 
to locating them faster?

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:19.710
<i>Th-There must be something 
wrong with your sensor!</i>

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:29.870
Manifest your tool, Odin!

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:30.690
<i>Right!</i>

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.140
Kuraokami, manifest your tool.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:37.990
<i>Very well.</i>

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.730
<i>It's catching up!</i>

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:46.630
Haru!

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.430
Ow...

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:55.280
Misapyon! What happened 
to your danger detection?

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:57.740
<i>Danger incoming!</i>

00:16:58.180 --> 00:16:59.970
Oh, come on, Misapyon.

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:02.010
What's the point of warning 
me after it's passed?

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:02.010
<i>Haru! Look left!</i>

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:06.040
You okay, Haru?

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.430
Thank you, Makimaki-san!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.720
Kazamatsuri?

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:29.000
<i>Namino, you okay?</i>

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.820
I could've handled that myself.

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:34.510
Ame-no-Torifune!

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.860
Let's show the young miss 
what real space fishing is like!

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:39.530
<i>Yahoo! You got it!</i>

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.920
Took you long enough, Kazamatsuri.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:44.870
Let's do this already.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.020
Roger!

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:48.000
Kissho, Golden Pigs!

00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:53.840
Today is your lucky day.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:08.870
Izanami, Supernatural Power!

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:14.940
Go play!

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:19.370
Ame-no-Torifune, Supernatural Power!

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:26.600
Ready for another day of hype!

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.090
Launching capturing net.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.690
Capture complete.

00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:42.670
Okay! Let's keep moving!

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.820
That's what real space-fisher 
teamwork looks like.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.520
<b>Warning</b>

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.730
<i>The lord of this tank has appeared! It's nearby!</i>

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:57.700
<i>Yer not hurt, are ya?</i>

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.780
I'm fine. Thank you.

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:02.400
What's going on? A quake?

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:07.630
<i>Thanks, Namino.</i>

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.420
<b><i>Megacrabite</i></b>

00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:17.680
Wh-What is this monster?

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:21.530
<i>We stand no chance against it. 
We should retreat.</i>

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:24.120
What?

00:19:24.590 --> 00:19:25.380
Haru!

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:29.830
Oh, no!

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.020
<b>Danger</b>

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.020
S-Somebody...

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.520
<b>S-Somebody...</b>

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.230
Save me!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:35.230
<b>Save me!!!</b>

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:39.530
It's gonna break!

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.000
<i>Don't worry. Help is on the way.</i>

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:43.890
Play some more!

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.710
I always knew there was something here,

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:54.690
but I didn't expect a Megacrabite!

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.670
<i>We need to use Divine Splash!</i>

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:57.670
<i>Shall we?</i>

00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:01.130
Supernatural Power Max Output!

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.350
Kissho!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:16.690
Izanami!

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.650
Ame-no-Torifune!

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:24.490
Hype!

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:26.120
Divine Splash!

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.790
Th-That's...

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:35.180
A Divine Splash.

00:20:35.180 --> 00:20:36.600
<i>That's incredible.</i>

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:45.600
In the end, the girls' squad 
couldn't catch a single fish.

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:49.430
It looks like girls really aren't 
cut out for space fishing.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:52.730
Sheesh.

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:55.440
You ruined one of our flying fish!

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:59.400
Do you get that you're 
nowhere near our level now?

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:01.690
Speak up if you've got any objections!

00:21:02.250 --> 00:21:03.910
Then let me say...

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:06.860
<i>Murakami Namino! Maki Makiko!
Soramachi Haru!</i>

00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:10.540
<i>How dare you go space 
fishing without my permission?!</i>

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.580
<i>And you catch zero?!</i>

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:16.410
Th-That's because Haru held us back.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:17.540
What? Me?!

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.140
<i>You're the one who dragged me here!</i>

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:22.690
<i>I dare you to say that again, 
you good-for-nothing!</i>

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:24.510
<i>Can you do anything other than complain?</i>

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:24.510
<i>There, there. Calm down...</i>

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.300
Shut up!

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:30.560
<i>I'm training all three of you from the ground 
up once you get back to Earth, okay?</i>

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:31.360
Me, too?

00:21:31.360 --> 00:21:33.190
<i>Obviously! We're done here!</i>

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.380
That was unexpected.

00:21:35.820 --> 00:21:37.310
Who was that, anyway?

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:38.910
It's all your fault!

00:21:38.910 --> 00:21:41.750
Come on. Don't be so mad.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:43.690
Let's do this the friendly way.

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:45.770
How are you still smilin'?

00:21:45.770 --> 00:21:48.070
I'm never teamin' with you again!

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:51.170
Ow! Say no to violence!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:57.930
<i>Grandma, I'm not gonna give up.</i>

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:01.500
<i>I swear I'll become a great space fisher!</i>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>The Girls' Squad Gathers!</b>

00:23:36.300 --> 00:23:39.060
Next episode: "The Girls' Squad Gathers!"
